# EdCoach AI - Development Patterns

## Master Context
📖 **All project context**: @docs/CONTEXT.md  
🎨 **Brand system**: @docs/brand-guidelines.md  
🤖 **Agent coordination**: @docs/agents/README.md

## Mission
Transform classroom walkthroughs into a **continuous, supportive, and data-informed growth loop** for educators.

## Essential Development Patterns

### Design System Integration
- **Design tokens**: ALWAYS use `lib/design-tokens.ts` (never hardcode values)
- **Components**: Build on shadcn/ui base, follow `components/ui/` patterns
- **Accessibility**: WCAG AA compliance throughout
- **Responsive**: Mobile-first design for tablet coaching workflows

### TypeScript Standards
- **Strict mode**: Use proper type annotations and Convex generated types
- **Component structure**: Follow established patterns with proper interfaces
- **Error handling**: Comprehensive error boundaries and user feedback

### Convex Backend Patterns
- **Function types**: Use `query`, `mutation`, `action`, `internalMutation` appropriately
- **Validators**: Implement comprehensive validation for all functions
- **Performance**: Optimize for <3 second load times and real-time features
- **AI Integration**: Handle OpenAI API failures with fallback mechanisms

### Next.js App Router
- **Route groups**: Use `(dashboard)`, `(marketing)`, `(setup)` organization
- **Loading states**: Implement loading.tsx and error.tsx for better UX
- **Performance**: Use Suspense boundaries and optimize for mobile

## Quick Reference
- **Continuous Growth Loop**: Set Goal → Capture → Generate → Reflect → Monitor
- **Performance target**: <3 seconds load time, <10 seconds AI generation
- **Primary users**: Coaches (tablet/iPad) and Teachers (smartphone)
- **Success metrics**: <5min walkthroughs, 90%+ completion rates

## Agent Workflow
1. **Product Manager** → defines requirements (uses @docs/CONTEXT.md User Context)
2. **System Architect** → creates specs (uses @docs/CONTEXT.md Technical Context)  
3. **UX Designer + Backend Engineer** → parallel work (use respective contexts)
4. **Frontend Engineer** → integration (uses all contexts from @docs/CONTEXT.md)

For detailed guidance, see @docs/agents/[role].md
